Web search results for query: "指値 待ち行列 FIFO 約定 バックテスト エンジン 板"  Links: [{"title":"スタック(Stack, LIFO)と待ち行列(queue, FIFO","url":"http://www.math.u-ryukyu.ac.jp/~suga/C/2004/12/node2.html"},{"title":"FIFO注文｜CFD取引｜SBIネオトレード証券","url":"https://www.sbineotrade.jp/CFD/order/fifo.html"},{"title":"FIFO（LILO / 先入先出法）とは - IT用語辞典 e-Words","url":"https://e-words.jp/w/FIFO.html"},{"title":"キュー（待ち行列）とは - IT用語辞典 e-Words","url":"https://e-words.jp/w/%E3%82%AD%E3%83%A5%E3%83%BC.html"},{"title":"株式の約定の仕組み | 三菱UFJ eスマート証券（旧社名：auカブコム証券）","url":"https://kabu.com/beginner/stock/contract.html"},{"title":"このチャートのすべてのストラテジーについてのストラテジープロパティ - バックテスト","url":"https://help.tradestation.com/09_05/monex/jpn/tradestationhelp/st_testing/strategy_properties_strategies_chart_backtesting.htm"},{"title":"TradingViewの指値を使ったバックテストについて｜はぐ","url":"https://note.com/tibita78/n/n1e3ff8909c1e"},{"title":"FIFO | 今更聞けないIT用語集 | 株式会社APPSWINGBY","url":"https://appswingby.com/fifo-%E4%BB%8A%E6%9B%B4%E8%81%9E%E3%81%91%E3%81%AA%E3%81%84it%E7%94%A8%E8%AA%9E%E9%9B%86/"},{"title":"バックテストプログラムを組むうえで注意すること | 【日経225先物】トレードシステム開発ブログ","url":"https://diy-tradesystem.com/auto/backtest/backtestnotes"}]  検索結果から、あなたの検索クエリに関連する情報が見つかりました。以下が主な内容です：  **FIFO（First In First Out）について：** FIFOは複数の対象を取り扱う順序を表す用語で、最初に入れたものを最初に取り出す方式であり、先に到着したものや登録されたものから順番に処理する考え方で、コンピュータのキュー（待ち行列）など様々な分野で用いられています。  **待ち行列（キュー）：** 待ち行列はキュー、キーとも言い、最初のものから順に使っていく方式で、FIFO(First In First Out)と呼ばれます。  **金融取引でのFIFO注文：** FIFO注文はストリーミング（成行）注文のオプションとして設定できる機能で、「First In First Out」の略です。FIFO注文を設定して注文を行うと、反対ポジションを保有している場合に保有している古い反対ポジションから順決済されます。  **バックテストにおける指値約定：** バックテストにおいて、指値注文の約定は必ず1ティック以上「突き抜けて」いなければ、約定したこととしてはいけません。  検索結果には、板（オーダーブック）とバックテストエンジンの具体的な実装についての詳細情報は限定的です。   REMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.

### [W-2] WebSearch「limit order fill queue position backtesting simulator FIFO market microstructure」(3036 文字)
Web search results for query: "limit order fill queue position backtesting simulator FIFO market microstructure"  Links: [{"title":"Same Book, Different Fills: Partial Identification of FIFO Execution from Aggregate Order Books","url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2609.13597"},{"title":"Queue Position Modeling - HftBacktest","url":"https://www.mintlify.com/nkaz001/hftbacktest/concepts/queue-position"},{"title":"The Negative Drift of a Limit Order Fill","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2407.16527"},{"title":"The Value of Queue Position in a Limit Order Book Ciamac C. Moallemi","url":"http://market-microstructure.institutlouisbachelier.org/uploads/91_7%20MOALLEMI%202014-12-paris-mm-queue-value.pdf"},{"title":"A Model for Queue Position Valuation in a Limit Order Book∗ Ciamac C. Moallemi","url":"https://moallemi.com/ciamac/papers/queue-value-2016.pdf"},{"title":"Probability Queue Position Models - HftBacktest - Read the Docs","url":"https://hftbacktest.readthedocs.io/en/latest/tutorials/Probability%20Queue%20Models.html"},{"title":"Latest: Same Book, Different Fills: Partial Identification of FIFO Execution from Aggregate Order Books · Issue #1530 · jjakimoto/research-issues","url":"https://github.com/jjakimoto/research-issues/issues/1530"},{"title":"pypi.org","url":"https://pypi.org/project/hftbacktest"},{"title":"github.com","url":"https://github.com/nkaz001/hftbacktest"}]  I found several relevant results on this topic. Here's what the search revealed:  ## Key Research and Tools  Execution simulators commonly separate two tasks: a statistical market model evolves the displayed limit order book, and a matching engine applies the exchange's price-time-priority rules.  ### The Queue Position Challenge  Level 2 (L2) order book data reports total quantity at each price but not the constituent orders, their arrival order, or which order a cancellation removes—missing details that determine when a passive order reaches the front of its queue and can be filled.  Prior L2-based studies pick one convention—front, back, or sampled position—thereby fixing one order-level history, such as when a child joins behind 300 shares at the best bid and a later 100-share cancellation may remove quantity ahead of it or behind it, resulting in identical L2 decreases but different fill probabilities.  ### Practical Backtesting Tools  HftBacktest is a high-frequency trading and market-making backtesting tool that accounts for limit orders, queue positions, and latencies, focusing on accounting for both feed and order latencies as well as the order queue position for order fill simulation.  HftBacktest provides sophisticated queue models to estimate your position and determine when orders fill, with queue position being arguably the most critical component of high-frequency backtesting.  It is essential for accurate backtesting to find the proper queue position modeling by comparing backtest and real trading results.   REMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.

